From: Raven maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: reap owned process during destruction

Destroying an isolated IPA proxy kills its worker but removes the pidfd
notifier before it can collect the exit status. Reconfiguring a camera then
leaves one zombie worker per session. Wait for the owned child after SIGKILL;
do not install an application-wide SIGCHLD handler or reap unrelated children.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Raven maintainers <74085717+Swamy-BV@users.noreply.github.com>

--- a/src/libcamera/process.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/process.cpp
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
 
 #include <algorithm>
 #include <dirent.h>
+#include <errno.h>
 #include <fcntl.h>
 #include <signal.h>
 #include <string.h>
@@ -118,8 +119,12 @@
 
 Process::~Process()
 {
+	pidfdNotify_.reset();
 	kill();
-	/* \todo wait for child process to exit */
+	if (pid_ > 0) {
+		while (waitpid(pid_, nullptr, 0) < 0 && errno == EINTR) {
+		}
+	}
 }
 
